    "issue_alignment": "Public issue: when a time format includes a year, the time string is passed directly to the parsing function (flb_strptime) without ensuring it is null-terminated, causing the parser to read beyond the buffer (heap-buffer-overflow). This candidate triggers it: LTSV log ends with time value '202' whose last digit is the final byte of the input heap buffer, so _conv_num's digit-test reads one byte past the allocation."
